| `D1_s1_disp_20260927_041648.vi` | The display-loop VI the last review demanded. ExecState 1, E3 6 == 6, saved by script. **Never run.** | `STATUS.md:12`, `STATUS.md:74-78` |
| INDEX row 57 | The ABBA that should have judged it. All 4 legs stopped before pick 1, every value `None`. Marked "NON-RESULT - never cite as data". | `archive/benchmarks/INDEX.md:78` |
| Cycle 107 ABBA retry | Leg 1 refused at the VISA precheck in 13 s, `counted_by_arm: {}`, LabVIEW never started. | `tools/bench/disp_107_abba.json:19,27,40`, `result_107-1.json:15` |
| Cycles 105–106 | The run stop was found: NI-VISA refuses the rotor port (`0xBFFF0072`) even with LabVIEW closed. A leg guard and stage tooling were then built. | `STATUS.md:59-73` |

The file is real progress over the last review's "no file". It is a structural artefact with no number behind it. By this card's own standard, "a VI exists" is not evidence.

